# Counterfactual for criterion 4 - is the widget test load-bearing?
# main @ 5c7603e

The criterion-4 widget test claims the stamp MOVED into UpdateTaskUseCase
rather than disappearing when task_detail_screen.dart stopped minting one.
A test that only asserts 'the screen has no DateTime.now()' would pass just
as well if the stamp were lost entirely. So: break the use case and re-run.

## Step 1 - remove the restamp from UpdateTaskUseCase (simulating the stamp being lost)
$ git diff --no-color -- lib/features/tasks/domain/usecases/update_task_usecase.dart
diff --git a/lib/features/tasks/domain/usecases/update_task_usecase.dart b/lib/features/tasks/domain/usecases/update_task_usecase.dart
index a0a064c..1a7e177 100644
--- a/lib/features/tasks/domain/usecases/update_task_usecase.dart
+++ b/lib/features/tasks/domain/usecases/update_task_usecase.dart
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ class UpdateTaskUseCase {
 
   /// Executes updating a task
   Future<Result<Task>> call(Task task) async {
-    final updatedTask = task.touch();
+    final updatedTask = task; // COUNTERFACTUAL: restamp removed
     return repository.updateTask(updatedTask);
   }
 }

